{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage","id":1089894,"title":"Changelings and the Digital Web (Mage)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T12:32:14-07:00","id":1089894,"title":"Changelings and the Digital Web (Mage)","content":"A place of the purist banality or an opportunity for a new Arcadia? I can't decide. Autumn Folk are likely gatekeepers either way. I don't have any information on Changelings in the Digital Web. Please discuss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3983-kingdavid","name":"KingDavid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:48:26-07:00","id":1089903,"title":"","content":"I think it's got the potential to be very Glamorous, but beware the Banality of the gatekeepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:16:59-07:00","id":1089950,"title":"","content":"It depends on where you are.<br /> <br /> Site, community, page, person, type of activity you're participating.<br /> <br /> You can find places infested with Banality others are beacons of creativity. Yet lonesome Autumn Person can go in and kill it in mere days.<br /> <br /> The place can be dead for years and single Dreamer can turn into a garden of imagination.<br /> <br /> Some places might have both, imbuing changeling with hope and making their metaphorical headache unbearable. That how quick is the information flow.<br /> <br /> But keep in mind, that Changelings cannot enter Digital Web, they have access to the only aspect of it: the Internet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What makes me curious is this... Could websites have their own digital Chimeric Reality and could Changelings interact with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-10-2017, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T08:54:50-07:00","id":1090744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1089950#post1089950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes me curious is this... Could websites have their own digital Chimeric Reality and could Changelings interact with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a paragraph about this in my section of chapter one, but due to word count I had to cut it at some point. The answer, had it remained, would be: Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:16:29-07:00","id":1090770,"title":"","content":"I think people are confusing afew separate concepts. In mage there's basically something like Shadowrun's matrix that has grown based on the internet. There's also you know the internet. They aren't 1 for 1 things. Its like how there's an Umbral reflection of a place, and Shadowlands, and a Dreaming. the Internet has a Digitial web reflection and potentially other reflections.<br /> <br /> Since the Digital web can be accessed mundanely presumably Changelings can us it, I'd imagine you'd need some interesting levels of actor and prop to do much though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:11:49-07:00","id":1090835,"title":"","content":"From VAs' perspective it's all part of a Digital Web. And it began forming way before internet first appeared.<br /> <br /> And Internet (<i>actually, all networks</i>) is a part of Digital Web. The normies and non-mages have a limited access to DW in both how they can perceive it and where could they go. IIRC comparisons with 2D and 3D may have been involved at some point with non-mages being able to perceive flat dimension of Digital Web compared to Mages seeing it in glorious HD1080 3D.<br /> <br /> Digital Web isn't Umbra, but rather something on edge between consensual reality and Umbra. <br /> <br /> So it's the Digital Web has Internet - not the other way around.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, we'll have to see what Digital Web 3.0 have to say about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:44:44-07:00","id":1090849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090835#post1090835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From VAs' perspective it's all part of a Digital Web. And it began forming way before internet first appeared.<br /> <br /> And Internet (<i>actually, all networks</i>) is a part of Digital Web. The normies and non-mages have a limited access to DW in both how they can perceive it and where could they go. IIRC comparisons with 2D and 3D may have been involved at some point with non-mages being able to perceive flat dimension of Digital Web compared to Mages seeing it in glorious HD1080 3D.<br /> <br /> Digital Web isn't Umbra, but rather something on edge between consensual reality and Umbra.<br /> <br /> So it's the Digital Web has Internet - not the other way around.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, we'll have to see what Digital Web 3.0 have to say about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And it might secretly be Mout Qaf too but that's not really important for purposes of Changeling.<br /> <br /> [quote Digital Web 2.0]The Internet we use in the<br /> real world is just like the one people access in the World of<br /> Darkness, but it's only a poor window into the magickal<br /> Web, and rarely if ever a concern to the Awakened. Sorcerers<br /> download news, check stock reports, and surf for erotica<br /> just like anyone else. Those who spend much of their lives<br /> in the Web, on the other hand, are experiencing something<br /> far different from that. Most magi never enter the Web; they<br /> use chat programs just like the Sleepers do. The recent<br /> Crash has changed that, though. It's made a lot of mages<br /> very cautious, but it's made just as many very curious.[/quote]<br /> <br /> the Digital Web is its own place, you can get there from networks but not every network is inherently going into the Web. There's also Umbral and potentially Dreaming Reflections of the Internet. They are somewhat different things, though reflecting a similar truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:55:50-07:00","id":1090882,"title":"","content":"If I were to do up Chimerical Internet stuff it would mostly be Far Dreaming reflections, with maybe some trods leading into really weird parts of the Deep Dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T14:58:03-07:00","id":1090883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090882#post1090882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to do up Chimerical Internet stuff it would mostly be Far Dreaming reflections, with maybe some trods leading into really weird parts of the Deep Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a digital trod in chapter seven as one of the examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:36:31-07:00","id":1090895,"title":"","content":"Sad, that didn't make into the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T15:48:36-07:00","id":1090898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090895#post1090895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sad, that didn't make into the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It did, in chapter 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:14:44-07:00","id":1092038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090744#post1090744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a paragraph about this in my section of chapter one, but due to word count I had to cut it at some point. The answer, had it remained, would be: Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question I think I asked somewhere in another topic.<br /> <br /> To target artificial, intangible stuff - which levels of which Realms would I need - examples might include radio and wi-fi, artificial light, difital constructs: OS, applications, files, accounts, AI. That kind of thing. I think, that quick and dirty answer is Nature 5 and Prop 5 accordingly, but it feels wrong on some level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:15:34-07:00","id":1092072,"title":"","content":"I would say just Prop 5 since they're human creations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:24:15-07:00","id":1092075,"title":"","content":"Well, except natural radio waves and the like. You could use Hopscotch with prop 5 to really clean up, the signals for radio telescopes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T13:31:46-07:00","id":1092079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090835#post1090835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Digital Web isn't Umbra, but rather something on edge between consensual reality and Umbra.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that would make it inaccessible to anything not Mage, because Mage is the only place you find consensual reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:39:12-07:00","id":1092104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1092038#post1092038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I think I asked somewhere in another topic.<br /> <br /> To target artificial, intangible stuff - which levels of which Realms would I need - examples might include radio and wi-fi, artificial light, difital constructs: OS, applications, files, accounts, AI. That kind of thing. I think, that quick and dirty answer is Nature 5 and Prop 5 accordingly, but it feels wrong on some level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say Prop for anything man made, nature for anything natural and if you AI is something cutting edge/magey or you want to do wierd stuff like what are the dreams of machines probably Actor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T12:55:42-07:00","id":1092441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089894-changelings-and-the-digital-web-mage?p=1090744#post1090744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a paragraph about this in my section of chapter one, but due to word count I had to cut it at some point. The answer, had it remained, would be: Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love a book dedicated to this sort of thing. New Fae associated with the modern world would be an amazing addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}